---
// How an O-ring seals: installed squeeze, pressure-energised, and extrusion with the back-up ring fix.
const panels = [
  { x: 0, title: '1 · Installed', sub: 'squeeze makes the first seal' },
  { x: 270, title: '2 · Pressurised', sub: 'pressure pushes it harder into the gap' },
  { x: 540, title: '3 · Too much gap or pressure', sub: 'it extrudes: a back-up ring stops it' },
];
---

<figure class="viz">
  <p class="viz-title">How an O-ring seals: radial gland section</p>
  <svg viewBox="0 0 810 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="ors-desc">
    <desc id="ors-desc">
      Three sections through an O-ring in a groove. Installed, the ring is squeezed between the groove root and the bore
      into an oval. Under pressure from the left it is pushed against the right-hand groove wall and deforms into a D
      shape, sealing harder. With too much pressure or too wide a clearance gap, the ring is forced into the gap and
      nibbled away; a stiff back-up ring on the low-pressure side bridges the gap.
    </desc>
    <defs>
      <marker id="ors-ah" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto">
        <path d="M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 Z" fill="var(--rd-blue)"></path>
      </marker>
    </defs>
    {panels.map((p, i) => (
      <g transform={`translate(${p.x} 0)`}>
        <text x="135" y="20" text-anchor="middle" font-size="13" font-weight="600" fill="var(--rd-ink)">{p.title}</text>
        <!-- bore (housing) above -->
        <rect x="20" y="40" width="230" height="40" fill="var(--rd-steel)"></rect>
        <!-- piston with groove below; clearance gap between y=80 and y=86 -->
        <path d="M20,86 H85 V160 H185 V86 H250 V230 H20 Z" fill="var(--rd-steel)" fill-opacity="0.75"></path>
        <text x="135" y="62" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" fill="var(--rd-ink)">bore</text>
        <text x="135" y="215" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" fill="var(--rd-ink)">piston</text>
        {i === 0 && <ellipse cx="135" cy="120" rx="40" ry="39" fill="var(--rd-ink)" fill-opacity="0.85"></ellipse>}
        {i === 1 && (
          <path d="M108,81 H183 V159 H108 Q92,150 92,120 Q92,90 108,81 Z" fill="var(--rd-ink)" fill-opacity="0.85"></path>
        )}
        {i === 2 && (
          <g>
            <path d="M104,81 H166 V159 H104 Q90,150 90,120 Q90,90 104,81 Z" fill="var(--rd-ink)" fill-opacity="0.85"></path>
            <rect x="166" y="81" width="18" height="79" fill="var(--rd-ok)"></rect>
            <text x="175" y="176" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10" fill="var(--rd-ok)">back-up</text>
            <text x="175" y="188" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10" fill="var(--rd-ok)">ring</text>
          </g>
        )}
        {i > 0 && [96, 120, 144].map((y) => (
          <line x1="35" y1={y} x2={i === 1 ? 88 : 86} y2={y} stroke="var(--rd-blue)" stroke-width="2.5" marker-end="url(#ors-ah)"></line>
        ))}
        {i > 0 && <text x="40" y="176" font-size="11" fill="var(--rd-blue)">pressure</text>}
        {i === 0 && (
          <g font-size="10" fill="var(--rd-muted)">
            <line x1="200" y1="86" x2="232" y2="86" stroke="var(--rd-muted)"></line>
            <text x="234" y="96" font-size="10">gap</text>
          </g>
        )}
        <text x="135" y="262" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" fill="var(--rd-muted)">{p.sub}</text>
      </g>
    ))}
    <!-- extrusion illustration in panel 3: a tongue of rubber forced into the gap, shown faintly beside the back-up ring -->
    <g transform="translate(540 0)">
      <path d="M184,80.5 C205,80 225,81 248,82 L248,85.5 C225,85 205,85 184,85.5 Z" fill="var(--rd-accent)" fill-opacity="0.35"></path>
      <text x="196" y="104" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10" fill="var(--rd-accent)">without it: nibbled</text>
      <text x="196" y="116" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10" fill="var(--rd-accent)">into the gap</text>
    </g>
  </svg>
  <figcaption>
    An O-ring is a pressure-energised seal. Squeeze gives it a starting contact stress; pressure then pushes it into the
    low-pressure corner, so contact stress rises with the pressure it is holding. The limit is the clearance gap: push
    hard enough and the rubber flows into it.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
